<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
        <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
        <EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules>true</EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);RS1038;RS2008</NoWarn>

        <!-- NuGet Metadata -->
        <Version>5.10.0</Version>
        <PackageId>LinqContraband</PackageId>
        <Title>LinqContraband — EF Core LINQ performance analyzer</Title>
        <Authors>George Wall</Authors>
        <Description>Compile-time EF Core LINQ performance analyzer for .NET: a Roslyn analyzer that catches N+1 queries, client-side evaluation, premature materialization, sync-over-async, missing AsNoTracking, raw SQL injection risks, and other DbContext query issues in the editor and CI—not production.</Description>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/georgepwall1991/LinqContraband</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://georgepwall1991.github.io/LinqContraband/</PackageProjectUrl>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>Six new rules, five with code fixes: LC051 reports ToAsyncEnumerable() on an EF Core query, which runs it synchronously (fix: AsAsyncEnumerable()); LC052 reports DateTime.Now, Guid.NewGuid() and similar values in HasData seed data or HasDefaultValue, which make every migration differ; LC053 reports a second unnamed HasQueryFilter that silently replaces a tenant or soft-delete filter (fix: merge with &amp;&amp;); LC054 reports Migrate() inside a user transaction, which EF Core 9+ rejects; LC055 reports an OnModelCreating override that skips base.OnModelCreating; LC056 reports LINQ composed over a stored procedure call in FromSql. LC042 now scores query shape instead of counting method names and gains a TagWith/TagWithCallSite fix. A new suppressor hides the .NET SDK's CA1862, CA1304, CA1305, CA1307, CA1309, CA1310 and CA1311 warnings inside EF Core query lambdas, where their suggested overloads cannot be translated to SQL. Fewer false positives: LC001 trusts LINQKit, NeinLinq, DelegateDecompiler and HasDbFunction mappings; LC001, LC004, LC016, LC020 and LC022 skip in-memory AsQueryable() queries; LC007 skips batch, polling and retry loops; LC017 treats entity writes as escapes; LC026 accepts CancellationToken.None; LC031 stops at project query helpers; LC045 follows ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly; LC018 and LC034 defer to EF Core's EF1002/EF1003 (LC037 is unchanged). Safer fixes: LC009 withholds AsNoTracking() when entities leave the method, and LC018 rewrites to FromSql. The documentation site now covers LC048, LC049 and LC050 in its guides.</PackageReleaseNotes>
        <PackageTags>efcore;entity-framework-core;EntityFrameworkCore;LINQ;IQueryable;NPlusOne;client-side-evaluation;AsNoTracking;DbContext;query-performance;roslyn;roslyn-analyzer;analyzers;static-analysis;performance;sql;csharp;dotnet</PackageTags>
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>

        <!-- SourceLink & Debugging -->
        <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
        <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
        <DebugType>embedded</DebugType>
        <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

        <!-- Analyzer Packaging Configuration -->
        <IncludeBuildOutput>false</IncludeBuildOutput>
        <DevelopmentDependency>true</DevelopmentDependency>
        <SuppressDependenciesWhenPacking>true</SuppressDependenciesWhenPacking>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="..\..\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
        <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
        <None Include="..\..\assets\**\*" Pack="true" PackagePath="assets\" />
        <!-- Opt-in severity presets (<LinqContrabandPreset>), generated from RuleCatalogPresets. -->
        <None Update="build\LinqContraband.targets" Pack="true" PackagePath="build/%(Filename)%(Extension)" />
        <None Update="build\presets\*.globalconfig" Pack="true" PackagePath="build/presets/%(Filename)%(Extension)" />
        <!-- Include analyzer DLL in correct path for Roslyn -->
        <None Include="$(OutputPath)\$(AssemblyName).dll" Pack="true" PackagePath="analyzers/dotnet/cs" Visible="false"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Analyzers" Version="5.3.0">
            <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
            <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
        </PackageReference>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp" Version="4.3.0">
            <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
        </PackageReference>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Workspaces" Version="4.3.0">
            <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
        </PackageReference>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="LinqContraband.Tests" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
